  "func": "min_window",
  "prompt": "Return the shortest contiguous piece of s that contains every character of t, counting repeats. If none exists return \"\". When several shortest pieces exist, return the one that starts first.\n\nSignature:\n    def min_window(s: str, t: str) -> str:\n\nExamples:\n    min_window('ADOBECODEBANC', 'ABC') -> 'BANC'\n    min_window('a', 'b') -> ''",
  "starter": "def min_window(s: str, t: str) -> str:\n    # Your code here\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "from collections import Counter\n\ndef min_window(s, t):\n    need = Counter(t)\n    missing = len(t)\n    left = 0\n    best = (float(\"inf\"), 0, 0)\n    for right, c in enumerate(s):\n        if need[c] > 0:\n            missing -= 1\n        need[c] -= 1\n        while missing == 0:\n            if right - left + 1 < best[0]:\n                best = (right - left + 1, left, right + 1)\n            need[s[left]] += 1\n            if need[s[left]] > 0:\n                missing += 1\n            left += 1\n    return s[best[1]:best[2]] if best[0] != float(\"inf\") else \"\"\n",
